From: Dhanunjanrao Katta <katta.dhanunjanrao@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Sep 2025 11:44:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 137/190] drm: xlnx: hdcp: Limit stack frame size to 1024 bytes

commit 7ff15c890438ce0de0061a230dbca0a0f457628d from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

Several functions in `xlnx_hdcp2x_crypt.c` were triggering compiler warnings
due to excessive stack frame sizes exceeding the 1024-byte limit:

    warning: stack frame size (1032) exceeds limit (1024) in 'xlnx_hdcp2x_tx_compute_hprime'
    warning: stack frame size (1040) exceeds limit (1024) in 'xlnx_hdcp2x_tx_compute_lprime'
    warning: stack frame size (1192) exceeds limit (1024) in 'xlnx_hdcp2x_tx_compute_v'
    warning: stack frame size (1216) exceeds limit (1024) in 'xlnx_hdcp2x_tx_compute_m'

These warnings were caused by large local buffers used for cryptographic
operations. This patch refactors the affected functions to use dynamic
memory allocation (`kmalloc`) for large buffers, reducing stack usage
and improving reliability in constrained environments.

All allocated memory is properly freed using `kfree` to avoid leaks.

